<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vincenzo I Gonzaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1562">1562</a>–<a href="/years/1612">1612</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Vincenzo I, Duke of Mantua</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vincenzo I Gonzaga was Duke of Mantua and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a> from 1587 to 1612. A lavish patron of the arts, he employed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudio-monteverdi">Claudio Monteverdi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-paul-rubens">Peter Paul Rubens</a> at his court, and in Montferrat he built the great citadel of Casale around 1590 to guard the duchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vincenzo-i-gonzaga.jpg" alt="Vincenzo I Gonzaga" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frans Pourbus the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Duke_Vincenzo_I_Gonzaga_with_the_Collar_of_the_Order_of_the_Redeemer.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
